@startuml
'==============================================================
' DESIGN SET DS1 - User Account Registration & Authentication
' Sequence: Register a new account and confirm the email address (Member only)
'==============================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam ArrowFontSize 9
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 10
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #333333
  LifeLineBorderColor #777777
  ParticipantBorderColor #333333
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  ArrowFontSize 9
}
skinparam ParticipantPadding 12

'===============================================================
' Every layer is a rectangle with a single head at the top.
' The life lines get shorter from the left to the right.
'===============================================================
hide footbox
skinparam ParticipantBorderThickness 1.2
title DS1 - Register a new account / Confirm the email address\n(Sequence Diagram - Member only)

participant "Member" as Member
participant "Register Page\n(React)" as Page
participant "AuthController" as Ctl
participant "AuthService" as Svc
participant "UserRepository" as UserRepo
participant "TokenRepository" as TokenRepo
participant "EmailService" as Mail
participant "MySQL\n(Database)" as DB

== REGISTER A NEW ACCOUNT ==

note over Member, Page : Only a Member registers here.\nA Content Manager or an Admin account is created by the platform administrator.

Member -> Page : Fill in the registration form\n(full name, email, password, confirm password)
Page -> Page : Check the form\n(password confirmed, strong enough, ASCII only)
alt the form is not valid yet
  Page --> Member : Show the inline validation messages\nand keep the form open
else the form is valid
  Page -> Ctl : Register the new member
  Ctl -> Svc : Register the new member
  Svc -> UserRepo : Look up the account by email address
UserRepo -> DB : run the query
DB --> UserRepo : the matching rows
UserRepo --> Svc : the account may already exist

  alt the email address is already registered and active or blocked
    Svc --> Ctl : Reject the registration\n(400 BAD_REQUEST "Email is already registered")
    Ctl --> Page : Show the error message on the form
  else the email address is free
    Svc -> Svc : Hash the chosen password
    Svc -> UserRepo : Save the new member\n(email, full name, hashed password, disabled, role MEMBER)
UserRepo -> DB : run the query
DB --> UserRepo : the matching rows
    Svc -> TokenRepo : Save a new verification token valid for 24 hours
TokenRepo -> DB : run the query
DB --> TokenRepo : the matching rows
    Svc -> Mail : Send the verification email\n"[CLH] Verify your account"
    Svc --> Ctl : Registration completed
    Ctl --> Page : Show the success panel\n"Registration successful!" and count down to the sign-in page
  end
end

== CONFIRM THE EMAIL ADDRESS ==

Member -> Page : Open the verification link from the inbox
Page -> Ctl : Verify the email of the member (token)
Ctl -> Svc : Verify the email of the member
Svc -> TokenRepo : Find the token of type VERIFY_EMAIL
TokenRepo -> DB : run the query
DB --> TokenRepo : the matching rows
TokenRepo --> Svc : the token may be unknown, used or expired

alt the token cannot be used
  Svc --> Ctl : Reject the request\n(400 BAD_REQUEST "The link is invalid or has expired")
  Ctl --> Page : Show the error message,\nthen count down to the sign-in page
else the token is valid
  Svc -> UserRepo : Enable the account
UserRepo -> DB : run the query
DB --> UserRepo : the matching rows
  Svc -> TokenRepo : Delete the used verification token
TokenRepo -> DB : run the query
DB --> TokenRepo : the matching rows
  Svc --> Ctl : The email address is verified
  Ctl --> Page : Show the success message,\nthen count down to the sign-in page
end

@enduml
